# 108: THE TENANT MAKES NOISE — a rig for the QSound EXTENSION (14z-108).
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. The roster's own voices live in DSP sample banks 0x80-0x8E,
# which are the CPS-2 WIDE QSound extension. The build's ledger says exactly
# what is there: 58 samples, image bytes 0x800000-0x8E5800 = 0.896 MB, banks
# 0x80..0x8E (tools/qs_ledger.py on the WIDE romset). On the MiSTer core that
# region is reached through slice D1's sample-bank WIDTH fix and slice D2's
# QSound SPLIT across two SDRAM banks (pcmh_sel = wide_en & pcm_addr[23],
# a 1 MB window at PCMH_OFFSET). NO SAMPLE FROM IT HAS EVER BEEN FETCHED on
# any FPGA implementation -- the last major subsystem of the profile at zero
# coverage (docs/project/mister_core.md section 12).
#
# WHAT IT DOES. 36_pick_tenant_cell's wheel walk to the tenant at cell 0x13,
# then 104_1p_auto_ko_win's idiom in the match: WALK FORWARD and MASH, so the
# tenant throws attacks that CONNECT rather than whiffing at range. Buttons
# 1-3 only and P1 only, because that is all jtframe v1.7.3's sim_inputs.hex
# can express (tools/rpl2siminputs.py refuses the rest, loudly).
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING A ZERO. A quiet run does not distinguish "the
# extension is unreachable" from "the tenant never made an ext-backed sound".
# That ambiguity is exactly what cost 14z-107 (12) an obj-bank-4 measurement:
# the replay put the cursor on Victor and the zero was true but meaningless.
# So this replay is written to maximise voiced events, and any zero result
# must be reported as AMBIGUOUS until a sound is proven to have been
# requested. The 36_pick_tenant_cell path is unchanged and MAME-confirmed to
# reach P1 +0x382 = 0x13 with the match live from ~2900.
#
# RIG CONFIRMED ON MAME BEFORE ANY SIM TIME WAS SPENT (14z-108): over
# frames 2955-3104 sampled EVERY FRAME, P1's anim_ptr takes 37 distinct
# values and P2's HP falls 0x120 -> 0x011b; across the whole window
# 2900-3600 P2 falls 0x120 -> 0x00ec. The tenant attacks and CONNECTS.
# NOTE for anyone re-deriving this: p1_attack_id at +0x0A reads 0 for the
# whole window even at per-frame sampling, so it is NOT the indicator to
# use here -- anim_ptr and the opponent's HP are. A 20-frame stride also
# aliases the attacks away entirely and makes a working rig look dead.
